**Package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`** (dir `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`) — pipeline functions plus helpers: `ValidateOwner`, `NormalizeOwnerAddress`, `RequirePostcodeForCity`, `RequireOwnerFields`, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, `RequireUniqueIdentity`, `RequireCityCapacity`, `RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`, `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`, `RequireDailyOwnerLimit`, `BuildOwner`, `AssignHousehold`, `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`, `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`, `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`, `SaveOwner`, `AuditOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `LoadOwner`, `ApplyOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `RespondWithOwner`, `DeleteOwner`, `ListOwners`, `ListOwnersPage`. Helper (non-function) classes in the same package: `EmailNormalizer`, `TelephoneNormalizer`, `AddressNormalizer`, `IdentityKey`, `HouseholdKey`, `CustomerCode`, `AgeBand`. Common helpers in `.../rest/function/common/`: `Strings`, `Luhn`, `Hashes`, `Localities`, `RespondWithNoContent`.

**`ValidateOwner`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwner.java`) — binds & validates the body once. This is the only step that binds `@RequestBody`; it republishes the DTO via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` for downstream steps:
```java
@Validated
public class ValidateOwner {
    public void service(@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated) {
        validated.set(request);
    }
}
```

**`NormalizeOwnerEmail`** (`.../owner/NormalizeOwnerEmail.java`) — the existing email step. It reads the shared DTO via `@Val`, leaves blank alone, throws `InvalidEmailException` (400) on syntactically-invalid, else writes back the lowercased value. This is the closest model for the new blocklist step (and the domain to check is `owner.getEmail()` after this runs):
```java
public class NormalizeOwnerEmail {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto owner) throws InvalidEmailException {
        String email = owner.getEmail();
        if (EmailNormalizer.isBlank(email)) return;
        if (!EmailNormalizer.isValid(email)) throw new InvalidEmailException(email);
        owner.setEmail(EmailNormalizer.normalize(email));
    }
