```

**`EmailNormalizer`** (`.../owner/EmailNormalizer.java`) — package-private final helper. Regex `^[A-Za-z0-9._%+\-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.\-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$`; `isBlank`, `isValid`, `normalize(trim + toLowerCase)`. Note the AGENTS convention: OfficeFloor requires exactly one public method per function class, so shared logic lives in helper classes like this. A domain-extraction/blocklist helper would follow the same pattern.

**`BuildOwner`** (create path) maps DTO → entity via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(request)`. **`ApplyOwner`** (update path) copies DTO fields onto the loaded entity, including `owner.setEmail(request.getEmail())`.

**Owner entity** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`) extends `Person`. Fields: `address` (@NotEmpty), `city` (@NotEmpty), `postcode`, `telephone` (@NotEmpty, @Pattern E.164), **`email` (plain `@Column(name="email")` String, nullable, no validation annotation)**, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `pets`. Standard getters/setters — `getEmail()`/`setEmail()` present. `firstName`/`lastName` come from `Person`.

